		<div class="methodology-intro">
			<p>Transforming 18th-century handwritten gothic ledgers into a structured, queryable database requires significant programmatic intervention. We utilized <strong>Python</strong> exclusively for data extraction, natural language processing, and spatial network analysis. Below are excerpts of the core scripts used to process the raw archival XML.</p>
		</div>

		<section class="code-section">
			<div class="section-header">
				<h2>1. Archival Data Extraction</h2>
				<p>This script parses TEI-XML transcriptions of the Moravian censuses, extracting demographic traits and handling missing temporal data via linear interpolation.</p>
			</div>
			<div class="code-block-wrapper">
